<title>GERMANY: HORSE RACING-RESULT OF GERMANY'S GROSSER DALLMAYR PREIS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULT OF GERMANY'S GROSSER DALLMAYR PREIS.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Grosser Dallmayr</p>
<p>Preis, a group</p>
<p>one race for three-year-olds and upwards, run over one</p>
<p>and-a-quarter miles (2</p>
<p>km) on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Oxalagu	    (ridden by Andrasch Starke)</p>
<p> 2. Dance Design     (Michael Kinane)</p>
<p> 3. Eden Rock	  (Torsten Mundry)</p>
<p> 4. Narrabeth	  (Darryll Holland)</p>
<p>6 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Half a length, three lengths, one length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Gestut Rietberg and trained in Cologne,</p>
<p>Germany by Bruno</p>
<p>Schutz.</p>
<p>Value to winner: $127,715 dollars.</p>
<p>TOTE betting (includes a 10 mark stake): Win 39; places 13,</p>
<p>11. Straight</p>
<p>Forecast 65.</p>
</text>
